            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0297" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg193"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3901: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-03T14:00:00+08:00">February 3, 1932—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 3—6:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Japanese Consulate General states that at 5:30 a.m. today when three Japanese
                    destroyers [were?] passing Woosung forts on the way to Sasebo they were fired
                    upon by forts. Fire was returned. Japanese Consulate General states Japanese
                    arranging to occupy Woosung forts.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation and Nanking for information.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
